// Boss encounter spec — GNU-ton, the scholar who rides the giant gnu.
//
// The scholar is the boss; the `giant_gnu` mount he rides is scenery you can
// stand on and cannot hurt (its arena placement stands it behind the playable
// plane), so there is no on-foot phase and no `mount_died` trigger. The phases
// are his lectures:
// Phase 1 "A Demonstration at a Distance" (the giant's arms are on it,
// and it punches through a pair of portals), Phase 2 "Lectures on Motion" and
// "Principia" (its arms are in two portals; its fists are bodies of their
// own), Enrage "The System of the World" — see the `gnu_ton_rider` row in
// `boss_profiles.ron`. The beat between phase 1 and phase 2 is the clamp.
(
    id: "gnu_ton_rider",
    name: "GNU-ton",
    max_hp: 42,
    // Phase 1 is a third of the fight (Jon, 2026-10-11: not a short phase).
    phase1_to_transition_hp: 0.64,
    phase2_to_enrage_hp: 0.28,
    intro_seconds: 2.8,
    transition_seconds: 2.0,
    // The launch into space before phase 3 (`choreography::space::LEN`): he
    // powers up, the giant lifts off, the sky goes to space.
    enrage_seconds: 3.6,
    // Music: Standing on Shoulders v2 as his adaptive cue,
    // `standing_on_shoulders_v2_adaptive`, bound to his phases in
    // `assets/audio/music_cues.ron` (`boss_bindings`): its intro one time, its
    // body looped through every phase, its outro when he falls. No simple
    // track per phase. The approach room plays the original (Jon, 2026-10-20).
    music_intro: "",
    music_phase1: "",
    music_phase2: "",
    music_enrage: "",
    // He speaks with the `npc_gnu_ton_boss` row's barks: Newton's voice.
    voice: Some("npc_gnu_ton_boss"),
)
